[Music]  6 42 it is time now for our weekly  morning cup of joe  with metro sheriff joe lombardo he joins  us live with his  cup of joe hey sheriff how are you  hey good morning out be here good to see  you thanks for joining us so early  what was that we have i think we got a  little delay going here i said happy  thanksgiving  it's all right happy thanksgiving to you  you know speaking of this holiday  weekend is going to be different of  course  is it different from metro's point of  view though and what is metro focusing  on this weekend  yeah it is the holiday season which  a lot of people travel i just heard your  broadcast a little bit earlier about the  increase in  an unexpected increase in numbers of  travelers during this holiday season so  in response to that we usually do a  pretty significant traffic enforcement  during the holiday season  to include aggressive driving speeding  and dui  so we have this program here at metro  it's called joining forces  as whereas all the traffic functions  on the local police departments north  las vegas nhp  henderson they team up and they do dui  enforcement and speed  infraction enforcement it's a pretty  successful program  as far as getting the the bad drivers  off the road and  hoping to curtail the fatal accidents  that occurred during the holiday season  so it's it's a big deal because you know  i was looking through some of the stats  associated with accidents recently and  the national highway safety  administration says that uh 40 billion  dollars  is associated to mitigating traffic  accidents associated with speed so it's  a big deal  so that's what we do  you know after thanksgiving of course we  have black friday and a lot more people  are shopping online this year because of  what's going on  so do you think package thefts will be a  bigger issue this year and what should  people do to prevent that  yeah i do absolutely i think i do well i  think i do i know i do  um i believe it is going to be a big  deal and it has been in previous years  with the proliferation of amazon and  and the ease of receiving items at your  house  but what people need to do is target  harden their own  residence or their own place of business  and you know advise your neighbor if  you're not going to be around or you  expect to receive a package or if you  have a security guard through an hoa  advise them and help maybe they can help  you you know a lot of these  folks follow the ups trucks and the  fedex trucks and  they do what they do they they see the  packets be delivered they follow behind  them and they go grab the package  and subsequently we get involved at that  point  it's important for people to target  hardener their  place of residence in other words have  their video cameras working that's a  definite assist for the police  department do an investigation  and it's important for people to be  aware of their surroundings so  don't make it easy for the crooks it's  unfortunate that people take advantage  of  people's uh um good will and charity  during the holidays  but we know that as a society we have to  deal with that on a regular basis so  it's important for people to be aware  that  and don't post your information on  social media like you're going to be out  of town  or something to that aspect to make it  easier for them  and hopefully we'll all be able to enjoy  ourselves yeah  it's so frustrating to watch those  videos and people even if they see the  ring camera or whatever camera you have  up and they still go and grab the  packages it's so frustrating every year  so that's some good tips all right  sheriff lastly here what other things  will metro focus on to prevent crime  during this holiday season obviously  it's going to be a little different in  terms of shopping and going out to malls  yeah but we still expect a lot of people  to hit the malls you know the brick and  mortar  business is still in business you know  some people aren't comfortable shopping  online  but we have a lot of crime issues in  proximity and the cartilage of the malls  and  shopping areas so with that with that  knowledge  we do very proactive enforcement in  those areas so we  we have the area commands uh concentrate  their efforts during the shopping hours  in the parking lots and with in a lot of  the places hire police officers on an  older time basis to police their  their businesses so we also put plain  clothes folks out in the parking lot  area so  i think it's important for people to  help us help them  and what i mean by that don't have your  packages stacked up inside your car so a  thief walking by could see them and then  eventually steal them if you have the  ability to  hide them in the trunk or the back seat  or take them home  as you go to and fro your your business  of the day  it's important for people to realize  that and be aware of their surroundings  when they're walking to  and from their car so they won't become  a personal victim  of a person attempting to take their  their gifts for the holiday season  yeah don't want that all right sheriff  we are out of time  it is great to see you have a wonderful  thanksgiving hopefully  your wife has some lovely food for you  tomorrow morning thank you for being  with us  uh thank you all right if you have a  question for sheriff joe lombardo  you can send it to us on our website  eightnewsnow.com  and find out if it was answered every  wednesday

